<title>FINLAND: Finnish finance ministry silent after S&amp;P visit.</title>
<headline>Finnish finance ministry silent after S&amp;P visit.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The finance ministry had no comment on Friday about U.S. rating agency Standard &amp; Poor's (S&amp;P) visit earlier this week but confirmed it had taken place.</p>
<p>&quot;I have no special comments to make,&quot; the ministry's Finance Director Kari Nars told Reuters by telephone.</p>
<p>&quot;Standard &amp; Poors were here...early in the week,&quot; Nars said.</p>
<p>Rating firms usually take about one- to one-and-a-half months to make reports after visiting countries, but case-by-case variation is significant.</p>
<p>S&amp;P's rating for Finland's foreign currency loan is AA-, and its outlook rose to positive from stable in August 1995.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
